/// This source winds a loop word at three lengths of cctt's
/// `tests/bench/s1.cctt`. There the winding transports zero along a word of
/// loops in the helix, and `forceℤ` forces the result.
///
/// gandr presents the loop space of the circle by its words. The winding of a
/// word is `wind`, which counts its letters. Each run writes the word, winds
/// it and forces the integer to `Tt`.
///
/// The run machine runs each length that this source states. At 10⁶ letters
/// the run spends its jump budget before it settles. With a larger budget, it
/// settles within `--memory 1GiB`. The machine does not run a word that
/// `Path.step` composes, because it does not lower that transport.
///
/// - see: #6309
/// - see: #6324 — the memory bound of the heap and the window region
/// - see: #6325 — the jump budget at 10⁶ letters
// The circle, its words and `wind`.
import "./circle-base.gandr";
// The numerals, `forceInt` and the loop words.
import "./ladder-base.gandr";

/// A word of a hundred loops winds a hundred times.
@[runs("Tt")]
def wound100() -> Top { forceInt (wind (loops n100)) }

/// A word of a thousand loops winds a thousand times.
@[runs("Tt")]
def wound1000() -> Top { forceInt (wind (loops n1k)) }

/// A word of a hundred thousand loops winds a hundred thousand times.
@[runs("Tt")]
def wound100000() -> Top { forceInt (wind (loops n100k)) }
